Assumption 3.2 (Approximate spectral decoupling). For analysis, we work in a basis where the data-
side covariances and the feature-side predictor operators are (approximately) jointly diagonalizable.
Concretely, we assume Σ11 and ΣX1 share an eigenbasis, and P := Wp⊤ Wp and Q := Wp⊤ M̄2
share an eigenbasis. This lets the coupled dynamics decompose into independent scalar modes.
The Assumption 3.2 is mild in the regimes we study. On the data side, when the context view x1 is
produced by mild masking, the cross-covariance ΣX1 is typically close to a scaled version of Σ11 ;
under common preprocessing (normalization), covariances are often near-diagonal. On the feature
side, P = Wp⊤ Wp and Q = Wp⊤ M̄2 are close to commuting when M̄2 is diagonal and Wp is
