6.1   Theoretical Motivation

We parametrize the predictor as a residual map, Wp = I + ∆Wp , ∆Wp ≈ 0 at init. Hence
the predictor Gram matrix satisfies Wp⊤ Wp = I + O(∥∆Wp ∥), preventing an arbitrary predictor-
induced contraction at initialization. In our spectral characterization, with Wp ≈ I, the initialization
regime becomes view-limited: σi is set by the masked-view energy Σ11 and γi by the view alignment
ΣX1 , rather than by predictor scale. To extend this identity-preserving strategy to the general
transformer architecture Vaswani et al. [2017], we must ensure the predictor block acts as an identity
map in token space. Standard self-attention initialization typically yields uniform maps (A ≈ N1 11⊤ ),
which averages out spatial signals and collapses µ. We propose ResidualPred, which enforces A ≈
I via a Diagonal Attention Bias. To prevent the internal attention mechanism    from    diffusing gradients
